07:43:43  INFO  [msg → human] I investigated the acm.org loading failure. The website itself is reachable, but the university DNS resolver is currently returning the wrong address for acm.org.

What I found:
- acm.org currently resolves here to 198.82.0.99.
- Connections to that address fail with “No route to host.”
- The Knowledge Plane traced this to a stale DNS override in the AS1 recursive resolver.
- The correct ACM service address is 198.82.0.1; when I tested using that address directly, HTTPS loaded successfully with HTTP 200 OK.

So this is not a problem with your laptop or browser. Administrators have already been notified by the Knowledge Plane; the needed fix is for them to remove/update the stale DNS resolver override and reload/flush DNS. Until that is fixed, normal browsing to acm.org may continue to fail on this network.
